    {
      "blockId": "tour:itinerary_text:fb5db666cae6efb7",
      "field": "itinerary.text",
      "sourceTextSha256": "9628c2c4cf2d3a96606667a57171a730d2d8fd8696ee0b2212ac886d1a064a2d",
      "text": "Visit the archaeological site of Quiriguá, an ancient Maya city founded by settlers from Copan in the second half of the 7th century. The park is a UNESCO World Heritage Site.\n\nExcavations among the tropical trees uncovered 22 monuments, or stelae. Some sculptures depict animals with human features, including a jaguar with a human face. The monolithic sculptures, weighing up to 65 tonnes, were carved without iron tools.\n\nAfter the tour, transfer to Honduras.\n\n**Overnight:** Clarion Copan Ruinas.  \n**Meals:** breakfast.",
      "provenance": {
        "kind": "ai_translation",
        "runId": "ada-en-mw2zik0k-amanda",
        "model": "GPT-6",
        "wordAbsenceReason": "The checked Word Quirigua paragraph lacks the assigned RU account of a seventh-century foundation, 22 monuments, a human-faced jaguar and sculptures up to 65 tonnes; these RU-only passages are translated without changing the source.",
